{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>They are frustrated</b> [—] <b>joy</b>: two [matters] joined." "<b>Counsel</b> — the matter of counsel. The meaning: others will frustrate the plans of those who plan, because there is no counsel; and through advisers the plan of those who seek counsel will stand, and joy will come to the man who counsels, when the answer of his mouth arrives."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 15, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:23:01.511195953Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}